From: akramboussanni <92455979+akramboussanni@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:16:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] macos: Connect with the link from Kimono Prayer

Why: the menu bar app reads everything through a person's own Kimono Prayer
link (https://<kimono>/api/v1/prayer/feed/<token>), which stands in for
signing in. Until it has one it can't do anything, so it asks for it.

What must survive upstream changes:
- Info.plist declares the mawaqit-kimono URL scheme (CFBundleURLTypes), and
  the app delegate's application(_:open:) hands
  mawaqit-kimono://connect?link=<urlencoded link> to MawaqitStore.connect and
  opens the panel. That's what Kimono Prayer's Connect button opens.
- KimonoLink.parse accepts either that address or the bare link pasted into
  the search field, and only http(s) links whose path is
  /api/v1/prayer/feed/<token> (query and fragment dropped).
- The link is SavedState.link, saved with the rest of the state file
  (Application Support, 0700 folder, complete file protection).
- Not connected: the search field says "Paste your Kimono Prayer link", the
  location button and its hint are hidden, and the status line asks for the
  link. Submitting anything that isn't a link just repeats that.
- Connecting replaces any saved place and calendar (keeping the notifications
  setting) and loads at once. Settings has a Kimono section with Disconnect,
  which forgets the link and the times.
- Tests/MawaqitMacTests/KimonoLinkTests.swift covers the parser.

